# {{projectName}}

A universal Expo SDK 57 application for Android, iOS, and web with Expo Router,
Firebase email/password Authentication, and per-user Cloud Firestore notes.
Scaffolded by dude's `expo-firebase` stack.

## Quick start

Requirements: Node.js 22.13+, pnpm, and Java 21+.

```bash
pnpm install
dude doctor
dude firebase emulators
```

In a second terminal:

```bash
dude dev --go
```

The default configuration uses the safe `{{emulatorProjectId}}` project and
cannot reach live Firebase resources. Open the Emulator UI at
http://127.0.0.1:4000, then create an account in the app.

## Commands

| Command                               | Purpose                                  |
| ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `dude dev --go`                       | Start Expo Go for Android, iOS, and web  |
| `dude firebase emulators`             | Start local Auth and Firestore           |
| `dude firebase deploy --project <id>` | Test then deploy Firestore rules/indexes |
| `dude build --platform <target>`      | EAS mobile build or local web export     |
| `dude lint`                           | Enforce RN and Firebase structure        |
| `dude test`                           | Run Jest and Firestore rules tests       |
| `dude review`                         | Run the full static review               |
| `dude docs`                           | Serve the project documentation          |

See `docs/docs/firebase.md` before connecting a live Firebase project and
`docs/docs/builds.md` before the first EAS build.
